WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.443
Welcome to Section Two: Planning.

2
00:00:02.643 --> 00:00:09.529
How do managers turn a promising idea into a service the
library can deliver, sustain, and improve?

3
00:00:09.729 --> 00:00:13.332
Meet Cedar Crossing Library, our fictional teaching
setting.

4
00:00:13.532 --> 00:00:18.557
An underused room could become a flexible place for
study and community learning.

5
00:00:18.757 --> 00:00:24.149
But some people need quiet, others need group space, and
staff time and money are limited.

6
00:00:24.349 --> 00:00:27.059
Our route begins with purpose and user needs.

7
00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:34.175
We gather evidence, compare choices, make a workable
plan, and connect space and communication to the
service.

8
00:00:34.375 --> 00:00:36.235
Then we evaluate and adjust.

9
00:00:36.435 --> 00:00:39.937
Every Cedar Crossing example and number is invented.

10
00:00:40.137 --> 00:00:47.597
This optional lesson supports Chapters Four through Six;
it does not replace the readings or your own case
analysis.

11
00:00:47.797 --> 00:00:51.930
You can listen, read, revisit, or skip activities at any
time.

